In wxWidgets 3.1.4, you can get column data from a column label string in a wxGrid by first finding the column index from the label, then accessing the cell value. Here are several approaches:

## Method 1: Basic Approach

```cpp
#include <wx/grid.h>

// Get cell value by column label and row index
wxString GetCellValueByColumnLabel(wxGrid* grid, const wxString& columnLabel, int row)
{
    // Find column index by label
    for (int col = 0; col < grid->GetNumberCols(); col++)
    {
        if (grid->GetColLabelValue(col) == columnLabel)
        {
            // Return the cell value at the found column and specified row
            return grid->GetCellValue(row, col);
        }
    }

    // Column not found
    return wxEmptyString;
}
```

